WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:08.040 align:start position:19%
when you get stitches a doctor threads a
needle through your wound and pulls it

00:00:05.359 --> 00:00:13.080 align:start position:19%
tight to close the skin as the stitches
hold the edges together the wound

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:18.480 align:start position:19%
becomes inflamed as new cells begin to
repair the tissue afterwards connective

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.279 align:start position:19%
tissues and collagens start to create
skin then blood vessels form to nourish

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:29.640 align:start position:19%
these developing tissues filling in the
area and over a few weeks the wound will

00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:33.000 align:start position:19%
have healed together and the stitches
are removed

